        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                "word": "понеже",
                "pos": "conj",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                        "entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "устар., канц. поскольку, так как, потому что"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "02e7b9fa-f7d2-4b87-990a-39b956d37424",
                                "sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                                "text": "Прежде, бывало, все распоряжения с «понеже» начинались."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "932396de-4722-4ccd-9250-2c80dcf18bbe",
                                "sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                                "text": "«Понеже» говорят подьячие в приказе: // Понеже без него не можно им прожить, // Понеже слово то показано в указе, // Понеже в выписке оно имелось быть, // Понеже секретарь им сделался в заразе, // Понеже следует везде его гласить. // Понеже состоит вся сила их в «понеже», // Затем и не живет у них «понеже» реже."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "cfd10c02-2fe6-40d1-a87b-c72637dfb32c",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                        "source_sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                        "target_lang_word": "since",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "since",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7d03f70b-f5bd-34cb-9047-96802e568c61",
                                        "entry_id": "a0168417-fe5c-3e68-b8f0-8f9aefa29add",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "From a specified time in the past."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9daf040b-2439-46bc-a121-e2188866bbe9",
                                                "sense_id": "7d03f70b-f5bd-34cb-9047-96802e568c61",
                                                "text": "I met him last year, but haven't seen him since."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e9fe88e-2745-4bf1-a0e5-796df20cbdb0",
                                                "sense_id": "7d03f70b-f5bd-34cb-9047-96802e568c61",
                                                "text": "A short/long time since"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "since",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d06ddb8c-53c4-363a-ad1b-c43c4d488413",
                                        "entry_id": "822830e2-b17e-372d-b0a5-aa093e7015e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "From: referring to a period of time ending in the present and defining it by the point in time at which it started, or the period in which its starting point occurred.",
                                            "Continuously during that period of time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3421fb05-a72a-4100-a796-d49425a89f40",
                                                "sense_id": "d06ddb8c-53c4-363a-ad1b-c43c4d488413",
                                                "text": "I'd known her only since the previous year, so from/since the moment we got married we’ve quarrelled."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "38d636b3-87d7-42d6-a697-b97ae5e42558",
                                                "sense_id": "d06ddb8c-53c4-363a-ad1b-c43c4d488413",
                                                "text": "I'd been working since six o’clock, and I was getting tired."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74a482d5-0731-4dae-9542-817d0810da85",
                                                "sense_id": "d06ddb8c-53c4-363a-ad1b-c43c4d488413",
                                                "text": "Since the mid-1980s, when Indonesia first began to clear its bountiful forests on an industrial scale in favour of lucrative palm-oil plantations, “haze” has become an almost annual occurrence in South-East Asia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3c178a8-185c-4c86-89bc-2ce738ae570c",
                                                "sense_id": "d06ddb8c-53c4-363a-ad1b-c43c4d488413",
                                                "text": "Since the 1980s, computers have had increasing roles in all aspects of human life—including an involvement in criminal acts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e3194da-93fd-33ea-9a50-1d4fb80b7c7a",
                                        "entry_id": "822830e2-b17e-372d-b0a5-aa093e7015e2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "From: referring to a period of time ending in the present and defining it by the point in time at which it started, or the period in which its starting point occurred.",
                                            "At certain points during that period of time."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebf7bf94-61de-4fa3-bd53-036e20887ef2",
                                                "sense_id": "6e3194da-93fd-33ea-9a50-1d4fb80b7c7a",
                                                "text": "\"Mujtahidd\" has attracted almost 300,000 followers since the end of last year, when he began posting scandalous claims about the Saudi elite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "since",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a45cbb9a-76a6-3806-8534-ffa7ff60d72c",
                                        "entry_id": "90d24c01-a5fe-388b-9e8b-5fca5b28fa09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "From the time that."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed34963d-206c-4554-9883-36c05b7eb60e",
                                                "sense_id": "a45cbb9a-76a6-3806-8534-ffa7ff60d72c",
                                                "text": "I have loved you since I first met you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e9b770f1-cf13-4de8-8f5e-51688b921b62",
                                                "sense_id": "a45cbb9a-76a6-3806-8534-ffa7ff60d72c",
                                                "text": "I've known her since I've lived in her street, but I've not seen her out of the house since her husband died."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fa12c1af-2ca3-4334-9aab-3eb2bc852f96",
                                                "sense_id": "a45cbb9a-76a6-3806-8534-ffa7ff60d72c",
                                                "text": "He had one hand on the bounce bottle—and he'd never let go of that since he got back to the table—but he had a handkerchief in the other and was swabbing his deadlights with it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "330dc66f-3dcf-32e3-aba6-41d6e917a6bd",
                                        "entry_id": "90d24c01-a5fe-388b-9e8b-5fca5b28fa09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Because."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c5cb614-20c1-4c6f-bf01-14b17e6889dd",
                                                "sense_id": "330dc66f-3dcf-32e3-aba6-41d6e917a6bd",
                                                "text": "Since you didn't call, we left without you."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "177433fb-fc95-4cf6-911a-7047255d9f63",
                                                "sense_id": "330dc66f-3dcf-32e3-aba6-41d6e917a6bd",
                                                "text": "The story struck the depressingly familiar note with which true stories ring in the tried ears of experienced policemen.[…]The second note, the high alarum, not so familiar and always important since it indicates the paramount sin in Man's private calendar, took most of them by surprise although they had been well prepared."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8be93c41-ef86-4480-b915-eba8177c8658",
                                                "sense_id": "330dc66f-3dcf-32e3-aba6-41d6e917a6bd",
                                                "text": "Since disbursement is the last step in the process of creating a mortgage instrument, the disbursement date may lag the transaction date by a considerable period."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "05822368-b24a-3035-85cb-9b66f29fe526",
                                        "entry_id": "90d24c01-a5fe-388b-9e8b-5fca5b28fa09",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "When or that."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d66c4fc1-4d06-4e20-87a4-98c19b38a964",
                                                "sense_id": "05822368-b24a-3035-85cb-9b66f29fe526",
                                                "text": "O ſir Iohn, doe you remember ſince wee lay all night in the Winde-mill, in S Georges field."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c49d126d-e73b-4d6b-b5e8-cdfab5a88933",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                        "source_sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                        "target_lang_word": "as long as",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "as long as",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2627d8ae-679b-31c4-b10a-c5667330401a",
                                        "entry_id": "a69b5240-dc9d-3801-a451-a07833c3fcfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see as, long."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc3f0515-b0ef-4de2-8362-a33d3a950b5c",
                                                "sense_id": "2627d8ae-679b-31c4-b10a-c5667330401a",
                                                "text": "It took three times as long as I expected (= three times longer than I did)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fff0b07e-4acd-3c5c-99f2-3a7a07b9abaf",
                                        "entry_id": "a69b5240-dc9d-3801-a451-a07833c3fcfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Provided that, if, assuming (depending upon some condition or requirement)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebf71eb3-ddda-4c88-8e19-1a6fe10037d2",
                                                "sense_id": "fff0b07e-4acd-3c5c-99f2-3a7a07b9abaf",
                                                "text": "I don't mind if he stays there, as long as he cleans up after himself when he's done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3d6dbcc-8c6a-4f37-aafd-09cb7c786f1f",
                                                "sense_id": "fff0b07e-4acd-3c5c-99f2-3a7a07b9abaf",
                                                "text": "I don't care who you are, where you're from, what you did, as long as you love me"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "809770ad-496a-37b8-aa70-b417880ef9ee",
                                        "entry_id": "a69b5240-dc9d-3801-a451-a07833c3fcfe",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "For the entire duration that; while; since."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "idiomatic"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b51e0f8-21ee-450e-85ae-b80c7088e696",
                                                "sense_id": "809770ad-496a-37b8-aa70-b417880ef9ee",
                                                "text": "As long as you're here, you may as well help me with the garden."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "as long as",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae88fc21-0a12-3d2d-b51b-1c6b65225bc0",
                                        "entry_id": "bc3b4f42-1e83-3302-bd45-ebd23cc37ee4",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used other than figuratively or idiomatically: see as, long."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "178ba44e-0e3c-4ea9-b79b-637e1ed599d6",
                                                "sense_id": "ae88fc21-0a12-3d2d-b51b-1c6b65225bc0",
                                                "text": "These meetings can last as long as three hours."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "15d7c5e1-fcbe-476b-b1db-ac919f4303f2",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                        "source_sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
                        "target_lang_word": "whereas",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "whereas",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1e399c14-4554-3837-b4de-ee4f733ef29f",
                                        "entry_id": "4b9b070d-acc5-30d0-ad7a-c80d1b3a0eb5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Where (that)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "538eb767-834d-48bf-a3b8-755d3fa86aae",
                                                "sense_id": "1e399c14-4554-3837-b4de-ee4f733ef29f",
                                                "text": "And home she came, whereas her mother blynd / Sate in eternall night […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whereas",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "745f0fee-3198-38fd-8a10-77b43ef0e6af",
                                        "entry_id": "7ddb29f8-1530-392d-bef7-569eeee90eb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In contrast; whilst on the contrary; although."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ace8977-d829-4108-9112-41bf7d488e7d",
                                                "sense_id": "745f0fee-3198-38fd-8a10-77b43ef0e6af",
                                                "text": "He came first in the race, whereas his brother came last."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "764fdbcf-b0ac-4a34-bafd-7197faac1736",
                                                "sense_id": "745f0fee-3198-38fd-8a10-77b43ef0e6af",
                                                "text": "One significance weakness of phrenology in the eyes of most anatomists, as Anne Harrington has shown, was that the brain comprised two structurally identical cerebral hemispheres, separated by a longitudinal fissure, whereas phrenologists held that the material sub-stratum of various mental faculties was located in only one hemisphere, and not its twin."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9775a96e-30aa-3ba4-8e97-a49e3c7da2a2",
                                        "entry_id": "7ddb29f8-1530-392d-bef7-569eeee90eb1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "It being the fact that; inasmuch as. (Often used to begin recitals; sometimes emboldened or emphasized as a signifier.)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1155ef3f-5e58-4b10-a24c-1eb381c52624",
                                                "sense_id": "9775a96e-30aa-3ba4-8e97-a49e3c7da2a2",
                                                "text": "And Whereas it hath pleased the Great Governor of the World to incline the hearts of the legislatures we respectively represent in Congress, to approve of, and to authorize us to ratify the said Articles of Confederation and perpetual Union."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "whereas",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "484a3adf-ed0c-388f-a7d5-fe8007624ccd",
                                        "entry_id": "cb8772c5-b6ac-3648-9791-cecd509db584",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A clause, as in legal documents, stating whereas."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67f1e904-19b8-45d8-9153-e8cba82ca4f8",
                                                "sense_id": "484a3adf-ed0c-388f-a7d5-fe8007624ccd",
                                                "text": "[…]the promise is stated after a whereas, though the promise is the very gist of the action, yet, such a count so framed, will be held good on demurrer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "069cacfa-d84f-4f92-a649-46121cd573d9",
                                                "sense_id": "484a3adf-ed0c-388f-a7d5-fe8007624ccd",
                                                "text": "It had a page or so of whereases."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "722d7779-5ec6-4829-a082-2312ad94651d",
                                                "sense_id": "484a3adf-ed0c-388f-a7d5-fe8007624ccd",
                                                "text": "I feel it is most unfortunate that some of the preambles, prefaces, whereases or whatever you want to call it, are put before motions or before resolutions[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "555cdc34-0a6c-4b0d-8ddf-65f4ee46b020",
                                                "sense_id": "484a3adf-ed0c-388f-a7d5-fe8007624ccd",
                                                "text": "If it is the desire of any Lodge on the floor that the whereases that were listed in their original Resolution be quoted by the Chairman or by the Secretary[…]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64949a16-907f-4896-96ff-776536a69330",
                        "source_entry_id": "0f991aeb-c38e-33ea-b0c3-dd8251a1a29e",
                        "source_sense_id": "71b0e78f-7bbd-3e4f-9e86-056e10bdb539",
